      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Finance networking is tight-knit.</strong> Miami's financial community is small and relationship-driven. The Greater Miami Chamber of Commerce, local alumni associations, and industry events like the eMerge Americas tech conference and Miami Finance Forum are the primary networking venues.</li>
        <li><strong>Latin American business fluency is a competitive advantage.</strong> Miami's international business orientation means Spanish fluency, familiarity with Latin American markets, and cross-cultural business skills are genuinely valued differentiators for many roles — not just token attributes.</li>
        <li><strong>Tech startup community is active but early-stage.</strong> Miami Tech Week, Wynwood-area startup meetups, and Endeavor Miami connect the startup ecosystem. Expect earlier-stage companies, more equity risk, and more generalist responsibility than in SF or NYC tech roles.</li>
        <li><strong>Compensation research must be Florida-specific.</strong> Using national or coastal salary benchmarks for Miami roles will create unrealistic expectations. Research Florida-specific salary ranges for your role and level on Glassdoor and LinkedIn Salary for accurate anchoring.</li>
      </ul>
